From 04129360f386701c6e37938eca42d069d070a782 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:46:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Annotation parts and board stamps: fix three review
 regressions

Review of 422817272d (PR #4054) reproduced three regressions against the
base. Each has a test here that fails without the fix.

1. stamp_boards kept session_external's own 5 s memo answer under the new
   board signature. When a commit removed the board's last scheduled card
   but other parked cards remained, the pre-commit external count was
   served until the board's next commit (base bound: 5 s). A read made
   under a known signature now bypasses that memo; the stored contribution
   is the only memo on that path. The memo still serves the
   unknown-signature path, as on the base.

2. The counts renewal read _cache_read_at, the active count slot's field,
   which belongs to whichever scope was read last. It now reads this
   scope's own read time (kanban_counts_scopes.read_at_locked); no counts
   for the scope means renew.

3. A wake for a scope with no demand dropped its clock deadlines but kept
   its part keys, so a deadline that came due in the gap forced nothing
   when demand returned. The keys are now dropped with the deadlines.

Tests: test_an_external_card_that_left_is_gone_on_the_next_request_and_
stays_gone (and the existing new-card test no longer clears the memo by
hand), test_the_renewal_reads_this_scopes_counts_age_not_the_last_scope_
read, test_deadlines_dropped_while_nobody_polled_force_the_read_when_
demand_returns. Without the three product edits: 4 of 18 fail; with them
18 pass. 182 test files that import the touched modules: 3306 passed,
0 failed, 1 skipped. scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks ok.

As deployed today the attention part is still read on every wake:
hermes-mods kanban-honest-done registers its done check with no watch
paths, so no key can vouch for it. Declaring them is the hermes-mods half
of t_28eb8d66d577eab3.

Hermes-Card: t_28eb8d66d577eab3
